            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial fibro-osseous lesion. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare tumor closely associated with the trigeminal ganglion produced a syndrome of atypical facial pain in a 44-year-old man. Two previous reports have designated similar tumors as &quot;fibro-osseous lesions.&quot; The distinctive morphological appearance is illustrated and possible histogenesis discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
